load @term/seed/code/structure/set
  find set

# The ternary heptagrid, the regular tiling {7, 3}, regular heptagons three to a vertex. It grows even faster than the
# pentagrid, and Margenstern chose it for the deepest theorem of the work, the undecidability of the hyperbolic tiling
# problem, because its structure hosts the mantilla, a recursive lace of nested interwoven triangles that can encode any
# computation. That it is hyperbolic is machine-checked by `seed test`. The form carries its set of tiles; its splitting
# tree and addressing follow the same method as the pentagrid.

# The heptagrid is hyperbolic by the Schläfli test: (7 - 2)(3 - 2) = 5 * 1 = 5, above 4.
hold heptagrid-is-hyperbolic
  call is-above
    call multiply
      call subtract
        code 7
        code 2
      call subtract
        code 3
        code 2
    code 4

form heptagrid
  link tiles, like set
